1 शुच् शो॑चति शो॑च˚ते (शु॑च्यति & शोचिति) flame,
light, shine, glow, burn;
 suffer burning pain;
 grieve at, mourn (acc.
±प्रति, loc., or instr.). C. शोच॑यति inflame, burn (lit. & fig. =
afflict);
 grieve at, mourn, regret (acc.). I. शो॑चुचन् etc. flame
brightly. — अनु grieve for (acc.), mourn with (acc.);
 C. = समनु
bewail, deplore. अप I. flame away, remove by flaming. अभि burn,
torment (also C. & I.);
 grieve, mourn. आ flame hither, bring by
flaming. उद् flame up. नि be burning hot. निस् flame forth. परि
feel grief or sorrow, mourn (absol. or tr. w. acc.). C. torment,
afflict, bewail, deplore. प्र shine forth (also I.). अनुप्र bewail,
deplore. प्रति flame against (acc.). सम् flame together;
 lament,
regret (also C.).

2 शु॑च् a. flaming, lighting, beaming (—˚);
 f. flame, heat,
sorrow, grief, pain, distress.

शु॑चि a. flaming, beaming (lit. & fig.);
 light, bright,
clear, pure;
 holy, virtuous, honest. m. purity, honesty, fire or a cert.
fire, a cert. month in summer & summer i.g., the sun, a man's name.

सूचि f. needle, sting, any pointed object i.g., pointer
i.e. index (in books);
 a kind of military array.

सूची॑ f. needle, sting, any pointed object i.g., pointer i.e.
index (in books);
 a kind of military array.

सुच्छाय a. affording good shade;
 well-shining, splendid,
beautiful.

सूचक f. सूचिका indicating, betraying (gen. or —˚);
 m.
informer, denouncer, N. of a man.

2 सूची॑मुख f. ई needle-mouthed, pointed;
 m. a kind of
insect or bird.
